cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "constellink: time-varying constellation contact graphs, routing and link capacity"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: AGPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/constellink"
keywords:
  - satellite constellation
  - contact graph
  - time-expanded graph
  - routing
  - link budget
  - free-space optical
  - forecast calibration
abstract: >-
  constellink computes contact windows for inter-satellite and
  satellite-to-ground links from sgp4-propagated element sets or generated
  Walker shells, assembles them into a time-varying contact graph, routes over
  its time expansion by Dijkstra, schedules an integer maximum flow over the
  same graph, and sizes each link with an RF or free-space-optical capacity
  model. It also ships a link-availability predictor with two deterministic
  baselines and a calibration-first verification harness. Research-grade
  software; not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational
  aerospace use.
